Article 73: The aims of the professional association shall be to:
1.   represent the collective interests of the covered entities, particularly in relations with the
government authorities and with the supervisory authority;
2.   provide its members and the public with information concerning every aspect of banking and
financial operations;
3.   conduct research into any questions of mutual interest;
4.   promote professional interbank training;
5.   organize and manage all interbank services, in agreement with the supervisory authority and under
its control;
6.   lodge a complaint before the courts in compliance with the provisions of Article 56 of this law.
